# Enforce LF line endings on checkout and commit.
#
# The toolchain assumes LF: oxfmt formats to LF, and scripts/validate-research.ts
# parses YAML frontmatter that silently breaks if a trailing CR survives a CRLF
# checkout (`status: draft` -> `"draft\r"`, failing prd.schema.json's enum). Without
# this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites tracked files to CRLF
# and breaks validation. `text=auto` lets Git auto-detect and skip binary files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Markdown is the most CRLF-sensitive surface (PRD + research frontmatter) — pin it
# explicitly so the intent survives future edits to this file.
*.md text eol=lf
